    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear directive: capitalize on favorable right-handed matchups to generate high-efficiency scoring. The primary anchor of the lineup is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who sits in the utility spot with the day\u2019s highest projection. His matchup against Feltner is ideal; the combination of a positive park factor and a weak opposing SP_xERA of 4.69 provides a massive boost, while his high sprint speed aligns perfectly with the team\u2019s priority to target scarce stolen bases. Following closely are **Christian Yelich** (73.18) and **Kyle Schwarber** (68.21), both benefiting from prime leadoff and two-hole spots against right-handed pitching. **Yelich** specifically sees a 13% boost from his dynamic platoon split, while **Schwarber** remains a lock given his elite xwOBA of 0.388 and the secondary order-position value.\n\nWhile the depth of the lineup is strong, we are keeping a close eye on **Kazuma Okamoto** (57.99) and **Lars Nootbaar** (57.09). Both hold sub-60 scores, placing them on the edge of our efficiency threshold, but they remain active due to favorable platoon advantages against Tolle and King respectively. The most difficult decision at the turn was bypassing **Jacob Gonzalez** (50.78), who provided the highest bench floor but ultimately lacked the upside of the starting infield. We opted for **Casey Schmitt** (56.25) over **Gonzalez** due to a stronger situational platoon edge against Holmes, ensuring we maximize our return on every plate appearance.\n\nRegarding risks, we are navigating a landscape where SP_xERA figures remain generally manageable, but we must stay vigilant for last-minute lineup changes. **Junior Caminero** (61.63) is our lone core starter facing a southpaw in Wrobleski, and while his base projection is high, his score is slightly suppressed by the platoon disadvantage. We are also benching **Dillon Dingler** (33.99) entirely, as his sub-40 efficiency score against Brown, H creates a floor risk that threatens our weekly games-played caps. Monitor the wind conditions for the **Schwarber** and **Crow-Armstrong** games, as any shift could further inflate their already high ceiling in this favorable environment.",
